      "content": "Your fear that support is meant to pacify you for labor is a valid defense mechanism when the world feels like an unyielding machine, but true belonging is rooted in shared humanity rather than productivity. Breaking this predetermined loop begins with small, intentional acts of defiance like setting strict boundaries, pursuing a hobby unrelated to your job, or redirecting your mind to practices like meditation that ground you in the present. You do not need a system to tell you that your life matters because the very fact that you question this cycle proves your inner life is still fighting for existence.",
